      "evidence": "DEDR 839 gives Tamil elumpu, Malayalam ellu/elumpu/eluṅku, Kannada elu/elubu/elugu, Kota elv and Telugu emuka ‘bone’. These forms are kept distinct from muḷe ‘marrow/bone’ and Indo-Aryan haḍḍa forms; the article's Sanskrit comparison is not asserted as ancestry. This is a comparative family proposal; inheritance versus local transmission in this survey lect remains subject to review.",
